.TH URNETWORK-VPN 1 "2026-11-04" "urnetwork-client 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
urnetwork-vpn \- URnetwork TUN engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B urnetwork-vpn
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B urnetwork-vpn
creates a TUN device, installs a default route through it and forwards packets
through the URnetwork peer-to-peer network.  It must run as root; normally it
is started by
.B urnetwork-connect vpn
or the GUI, which handle the route journal, the IPv6 block and cleanup.
.PP
On start it prints
.I "VPN connected. TUN: <name>, IP: <addr>"
and a periodic statistics line.  Pressing Ctrl+C, SIGTERM or a fatal engine
error tears the tunnel down and restores the routes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --api-url URL
API endpoint (env
.IR API_URL ,
default https://api.bringyour.com).
.TP
.B --platform-url URL
Platform endpoint (env
.IR PLATFORM_URL ).
.TP
.B --user-auth EMAIL
Account name (env
.IR USER_AUTH ).
.TP
.B --password PASSWORD
Password (env
.IR PASSWORD ).
.TP
.B --provider-id ID
Deprecated provider selector.
.TP
.B --country NAME
Exit country.
.TP
.B --city NAME
Exit city.
.TP
.B --region NAME
Exit region.
.TP
.B --mtu N
Tunnel MTU, 576..9000 (default 1400).
.TP
.B --tun-name NAME
TUN interface name (default
.IR urnetwork ).
.TP
.B --tun-addr CIDR
Tunnel IPv4 address (default 10.0.0.1/24).
.TP
.B --bypass CIDR
Extra destination routed outside the tunnel (repeatable).
.TP
.B --no-route
Do not touch the default route (for manual setups).
.TP
.B --block-ipv6
Add an IPv6 blackhole route so IPv6 traffic cannot leak (default true).
.TP
.B --replace-tun
Delete an existing TUN device instead of refusing to start.
.TP
.B --send-workers N
Number of packet sender goroutines (default 1 preserves ordering).
.TP
.B --send-queue N
Size of the bounded send queue (default 2048).
.TP
.B --verbose
Log every packet (slow; troubleshooting only).
.TP
.B --state-file PATH
Write engine state as JSON (env
.IR URNETWORK_STATE_FILE ).
When the engine runs as root, only paths inside the invoking user's
configuration directory are accepted; other paths are ignored and
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/state.json
is used instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list-locations
Print the countries, regions and cities offered by the network and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero on invalid MTU, missing credentials, unavailable exit location or a
failed engine.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR urnetwork-connect (1),
.BR urnetwork-gui (1)
